solutions.latex:
\exfigure{355_q12_s1}

Multiplying along the branches:
$$\begin{aligned}P(JJ)&=0.18 &P(JAJ)&=0.048 &P(JAA)&=0.072\\P(AJJ)&=0.168 &P(AJA)&=0.112 &P(AA)&=0.42\end{aligned}$$

Let $X$ be the number of spaces moved forward. An even roll gives $0$ (probability $\dfrac{1}{2}$), and each of $1$, $3$, $5$ has probability $\dfrac{1}{6}$:

\extable{Ts2678_1}
$$\begin{aligned} E(X) &= (0)\left(\dfrac{1}{2}\right)+(1)\left(\dfrac{1}{6}\right)+(3)\left(\dfrac{1}{6}\right)+(5)\left(\dfrac{1}{6}\right) \\ &= \dfrac{9}{6} \\ &= \dfrac{3}{2} \end{aligned}$$

